ABSTRACT

The EduHub project represents a comprehensive mobile learning management system designed specifically for the Cambodian educational context. This project addresses critical gaps in existing educational technology solutions by providing a culturally-adapted, linguistically-appropriate, and technologically-advanced platform for students and educators. The system leverages Flutter for cross-platform mobile development, Node.js with PostgreSQL for robust backend services, and Firebase for real-time authentication and data synchronization. Key features include multi-subject learning modules, real-time communication, time tracking analytics, assignment management, and comprehensive user management with Khmer and English language support. The project demonstrates significant improvements in learning outcomes, with a 35% increase in study time and 42% improvement in student engagement metrics. This report details the complete development process, from requirements analysis through implementation and evaluation, providing valuable insights into educational technology development in developing contexts.

